course: dictionary
lesson: 2813
title: Distract and its two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Distract means to take someone's attention away from what they should be doing or looking at. Look at the clues: «Phones, noise and chatting distract you from learning.» The phone pulls your mind away from the lesson, so distract means to pull your attention away.
explain: The second meaning is gentler. To distract someone can mean to get them interested in something else, so they stop thinking about something sad or painful. «Play specialists use dolls and games to distract children during procedures» means the games take the children's minds off what is happening.
explain: Always check by swapping in your meaning. In «Never distract a driver», you could say "Never take a driver's attention away", and it still makes sense. The clues are a driver and a road, which tell you it is dangerous.
explain: Distract changes its form: distracts, distracted, distracting. If you are «easily distracted», your attention wanders away quickly. A person who is distracted is not paying full attention right now.
fact: Distract is a verb, so its forms are distract, distracts, distracted and distracting.
fact: «Distract» means to take someone's attention away from what they should be doing or looking at.
fact: «Distract» can also mean to get someone interested in something else, so they stop thinking about something sad or painful.
fact: «Get distracted» means your attention wanders away from what you should be doing.
fact: Safety rule: never distract a driver or someone crossing a road, and put your phone away when you cross.
exercise: «Phones, noise and chatting distract you from learning.» What does distract mean here? | To make a loud sound | To fix a broken chair | To help you learn faster | *To take your attention away from your work
exercise: Why should you put your phone away when you cross the road? | Because it helps you run faster | *Because it can distract you from the traffic | Because phones are too heavy to carry | Because the road is made of phones
exercise: «The lizard's tail wriggles to distract the attacker.» What is the wriggling tail doing? | It makes the lizard sleepy | *It takes the attacker's attention away | It turns into a leg | It tells the lizard where to go
test: Which phrase means someone's attention wanders quickly? | *Easily distracted | Easily cleaned | Easily broken | Easily frightened
test: «Saying sorry after every mistake can distract the team.» What does distract mean here? | Makes the team run faster | *Takes the team's attention away from their work | Makes the team feel proud | Gives the team a new game
exam: Which sentence uses distract in the sense of getting someone thinking about something else so they stop feeling sad or hurt? | The phone on the table will distract the whole class | The teacher asked us not to distract each other with chatting | Please do not distract the driver on the road | *Play specialists use games to distract children during procedures
